Q1: Do people unknowingly pay $22 when minting costs $15?
A: No, they get refunded! Here's what happens:
User sends ~0.0072 ETH (~$22)
Contract swaps to ~$22 USDC
Contract uses $15 USDC for minting
Contract refunds ~$7 USDC to user

I already coded this contract (lines 265-269):
// Refund excess USDC if any
if (usdcReceived &gt; MINT\_PRICE) {
uint256 excess = usdcReceived - MINT\_PRICE;
require(usdc.transfer(msg.sender, excess), "Excess refund failed");
}

